            <ArticleTitle>Reversible coronary artery kinking caused by cardiopulmonary support.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>273-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Cardiopulmonary support is utilized to provide optimal hemodynamic stability in high risk patients undergoing percutaneous transluminal coronary angioplasty. This report describes a patient undergoing supported angioplasty in whom multiple new severe stenoses were noted following coronary dilation and that were completely reversed by discontinuing cardiopulmonary support.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
